description: WebAPI controller and DTO conventions
globs: SET.WebAPI/Controllers/**/*.cs,SET.WebAPI/Models/**/*.cs,SET.WebAPI/Helpers/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

# API controllers

- Inherit `BaseController`; inject via `IServiceProvider` and resolve services in the ctor
- Wrap actions in `TryCatchAsync` (user-scoped overload for authenticated work)
- Prefer `[Authorize(AuthenticationSchemes = JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)]` on controllers that touch user data
- Routes: `[Route("api/…")]` + `[ApiController]`; keep verbs REST-shaped (`HttpGet`/`Post`/`Put`/`Delete`)
- Validation failures return `BadRequest("PascalCaseToken")` matching existing style
- Scope queries with `user.Id`; never trust client-supplied user ids for ownership
- Prefer `DefaultConfigureAwait()` on awaited EF/async calls (project extension)
- DTOs in `SET.WebAPI/Models`; map with helpers or AutoMapper — do not return EF entities
- AI: keep prompts bounded; never expose `AI_API_KEY` to clients
